{
  "note": "The Functions of Sleep",
  "source": "5e5d2efa7fbb",
  "script": "bfd2b5da246e",
  "voice": "Patrick - Engaging and Warm",
  "model": "eleven_v4",
  "fingerprint": "a072d6cf33dd",
  "duration": 189.1,
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Functions of Sleep",
      "start": 0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Sleep has no single agreed function.",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.68
        },
        {
          "text": "Its purposes are therefore inferred largely from what happens when it is lost.",
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 7.28
        },
        {
          "text": "Two states are central here, slow wave sleep and rapid eye movement sleep, which is known as REM sleep.",
          "start": 7.52,
          "end": 13.88
        },
        {
          "text": "Both show a rebound increase following deprivation, and that rebound is the key evidence that both states are needed.",
          "start": 14.08,
          "end": 21
        },
        {
          "text": "What's more, each stage apparently answers a different need.",
          "start": 21.2,
          "end": 25
        },
        {
          "text": "We'll weigh up the evidence that sleep is needed, look at what REM sleep does, and then finish with slow wave sleep.",
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 31.28
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Evidence that sleep is needed",
      "start": 32.131,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Consider first what happens when sleep is lost.",
          "start": 32.131,
          "end": 35.251
        },
        {
          "text": "The missing stages are repaid at the next opportunity.",
          "start": 35.291,
          "end": 38.771
        },
        {
          "text": "Both slow wave sleep and REM sleep show a rebound increase following deprivation, rising above their usual levels.",
          "start": 38.851,
          "end": 46.451
        },
        {
          "text": "Such compensation implies that each stage is regulated and required, rather than optional.",
          "start": 46.531,
          "end": 52.211
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "REM sleep",
      "start": 52.976,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Turning now to REM sleep, selective deprivation of this state causes abnormalities in sensory processing.",
          "start": 52.976,
          "end": 59.669
        },
        {
          "text": "Subtle emotional and personality disturbances follow as well.",
          "start": 59.723,
          "end": 63.496
        },
        {
          "text": "These deficits point to a role in mind maintenance.",
          "start": 63.536,
          "end": 66.936
        },
        {
          "text": "REM brings repeated bouts of cortical activation, close to waking levels.",
          "start": 66.976,
          "end": 71.483
        },
        {
          "text": "The proposal is that this activity keeps the machinery of perception, emotion and personality in working order.",
          "start": 71.509,
          "end": 77.936
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, these are precisely the faculties that falter when REM is lost.",
          "start": 78.016,
          "end": 82.616
        },
        {
          "text": "REM is also proposed to be necessary for the consolidation of memories.",
          "start": 82.656,
          "end": 86.696
        },
        {
          "text": "Removing REM after learning impairs later recall.",
          "start": 86.736,
          "end": 90.096
        },
        {
          "text": "That is evidence that memory traces laid down while awake are stabilised during these episodes.",
          "start": 90.176,
          "end": 95.696
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Slow wave sleep",
      "start": 96.209,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Slow wave sleep, by contrast, is the phase linked to body maintenance.",
          "start": 96.209,
          "end": 101.036
        },
        {
          "text": "Within it, the deepest slow wave sleep is the part that really matters.",
          "start": 101.142,
          "end": 105.369
        },
        {
          "text": "Three things happen during slow wave sleep.",
          "start": 105.409,
          "end": 108.089
        },
        {
          "text": "First, hormones that stimulate protein synthesis are released, driving growth and tissue repair.",
          "start": 108.129,
          "end": 114.249
        },
        {
          "text": "Second, glymphatic clearance increases, washing metabolic waste out of the brain.",
          "start": 114.289,
          "end": 119.609
        },
        {
          "text": "Third, the immune system is stimulated, which aids defence and recovery.",
          "start": 119.649,
          "end": 124.409
        },
        {
          "text": "Consistent with this restorative role, the stage called N three is increased after exercise.",
          "start": 124.449,
          "end": 130.329
        },
        {
          "text": "N three is the deepest stage in the current three-stage nomenclature for non-REM sleep.",
          "start": 130.369,
          "end": 135.609
        },
        {
          "text": "It merges the former stages three and four.",
          "start": 135.649,
          "end": 138.729
        },
        {
          "text": "In other words, the stage four of older usage is the N three of today.",
          "start": 138.769,
          "end": 143.529
        },
        {
          "text": "Its rise after physical exertion ties the deepest sleep directly to the recovery needs of the body.",
          "start": 143.569,
          "end": 149.569
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Summary",
      "start": 150.335,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Taken together, both states rebound after deprivation, yet they do different work.",
          "start": 150.335,
          "end": 156.415
        },
        {
          "text": "REM sleep serves the mind.",
          "start": 156.535,
          "end": 158.535
        },
        {
          "text": "Its loss brings abnormalities in sensory processing, along with subtle emotional and personality disturbances.",
          "start": 158.575,
          "end": 165.535
        },
        {
          "text": "It is credited with both mind maintenance and memory consolidation.",
          "start": 165.575,
          "end": 169.882
        },
        {
          "text": "Slow wave sleep, meanwhile, serves the body.",
          "start": 169.988,
          "end": 172.935
        },
        {
          "text": "It does so through hormones that stimulate protein synthesis, through glymphatic clearance and through immune stimulation.",
          "start": 172.975,
          "end": 179.895
        },
        {
          "text": "Its deepest stage, N three, rises after exercise.",
          "start": 179.935,
          "end": 184.135
        },
        {
          "text": "In short, REM sleep tends the mind, while slow wave sleep tends the body.",
          "start": 184.175,
          "end": 189.135
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
